items.fromString:
Skupper does not support WATCH_NAMESPACE with multiple namespaces. It is either all or only one.

For example, all namespaces:

 
{code:java}
env:
  - name: WATCH_NAMESPACE 
    value: '' {code}
Can this be made possible?
{code:java}
env:
  - name: WATCH_NAMESPACE
    value: 'namespace-a,namespace-b,namespace-c' {code}

items.toString:
Skupper does not support WATCH_NAMESPACE with multiple namespaces. It is either all or only one.

For example, all namespaces:
{code:java}
env:
  - name: WATCH_NAMESPACE 
    value: '' {code}
Can this be made possible?
{code:java}
env:
  - name: WATCH_NAMESPACE
    value: 'namespace-a,namespace-b,namespace-c' {code}

The *Collector* component in the network observer system is responsible for gathering and managing vanflow records from remote sources across the application network and is non-deterministic. This might occasionally result in the Console reporting incorrect traffic. 

To workaround this issue you can restart the deployment with:


{code}
# Replace <your-namespace> with the site namespace.
kubectl rollout restart deployment skupper-network-observer -n <your-namespace>

{code}

